course: dictionary
lesson: 15208
title: Semiconductors: the in-between materials
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Some materials let electricity flow easily. These are conductors, like metals. Others stop it completely. These are insulators, like plastic and rubber. A semiconductor sits in between: it lets some electricity flow, but not as well as a metal.
explain: The name gives a clue. «Semi» means half or partly, and «conductor» is something that carries electricity. So a semiconductor is a partly-conducting material. Its flow of electricity can also be controlled, which makes it very useful.
explain: «The chip inside my tablet is a semiconductor.» Here the word means a small device made from this kind of material. Engineers in the semiconductor industry make these chips for phones, cars and computers.
fact: A semiconductor is a material that lets electricity flow better than an insulator but not as well as a metal.
fact: Silicon is a common material used to make semiconductors.
fact: The flow of electricity in a semiconductor can be controlled, which is why it is used in chips.
fact: A «semiconductor chip» is a small device made from semiconductor material, used in computers and phones.
fact: Countries such as Taiwan, South Korea and the USA make many semiconductors.
exercise: «The chip in my phone is a semiconductor, made from silicon.» What material is the chip made from? | Glass | Copper | *Silicon | Rubber
exercise: «Metals are conductors, plastic is an insulator, and a semiconductor is in between.» Where does a semiconductor sit on this scale? | Above all metals, as the best conductor | *Between conductors and insulators | Only in water | Inside rubber, as a kind of insulator
exercise: Where would you find «semiconductor chips» in everyday life? | In a book of poems | Growing in a garden | *Inside computers and phones | In a fish tank
test: «Countries such as Taiwan and South Korea make many semiconductor chips.» What are these chips mainly used in? | Keeping houses warm in winter | Growing crops on farms | Making bread | *Computers and phones
test: Why is a semiconductor not the same as a metal? | *It lets electricity flow less easily than a metal | It only works in water | It never lets any electricity through | It lets electricity flow better than a metal
exam: «A semiconductor's flow of electricity can be controlled, which is why it is so useful in computers.» Why is a semiconductor useful in computers? | *Its flow of electricity can be controlled | It never lets any electricity through | It is as good as a metal at carrying electricity | It only works in water
